# Frontend environment — copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and edit.
#
# Nothing here is required: every value has a working default. Only `VITE_`-prefixed variables
# reach the browser, and everything in this file is public by construction — never put a secret
# in it.
#
# `npm run dev` TALKS TO THE REAL BACKEND. There is no mock mode: the MSW layer that used to
# serve /api/v1 from fixtures was removed once the API was complete, so the dev loop now needs
# `docker compose up` at the repo root and a company provisioned with `provision-company`. Sign
# in with a real invitation-activated account.

# Where the dev server proxies /api. Only read by vite.config.ts, only in dev.
VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8080

# Which port `npm run dev` binds. The port is STRICT — vite refuses to start rather than
# walking to the next free one, because a silently-shifted port is indistinguishable from a
# backend defect once invitation links point at the port you thought you had.
#
# For a second concurrent lane use `npm run dev:lane-b` (6173, proxying to the lane-B backend
# on 9080) alongside `docker compose --env-file .env.lane-b up`. See
# docs/plans/2026-07-31-parallel-execution-rework.md.
# VITE_DEV_PORT=5173

# Identifies the build a tab is running, for version-skew detection. CI should pass the
# commit SHA; locally a timestamp is generated when this is unset.
# VITE_BUILD_ID=
